"Description: Element-wise logical NOT on a tensor (0 becomes 1, non-zero "
"becomes 0). Corresponds to Python's `not` keyword -- Triton handles this "
"specially through an AST visitor, rewriting `not X` as `X.__not__()`. Unlike"
" bitwise inversion `~X` (see [invert](./invert.md)): the former is logical "
"NOT, the latter is bitwise inversion."


